/**
 * @page model_selection_chapter Model selection and validation
 *
 * @ref ModelSelection separates configuration generation from configuration
 * evaluation. A @ref ConfigurationSelector implements an ask--tell stream;
 * @ref ModelSelectionFunctions supplies validation, final retraining, and test
 * callbacks. @ref ModelSelectionState retains only successfully scored records.
 *
 * @image html model_selection_components.svg "Model-selection components, ownership, and data products."
 *
 * @section selection_sequence Selection sequence
 *
 * @image html model_selection_sequence.svg "Configuration batch evaluation, feedback, and final model production."
 *
 * 1. The remaining `ModelSelectionBudgetCriterionConfiguration` allowance, when
 *    present, limits the next `ConfigurationSelector::ask()` request. The
 *    selector must return a non-empty batch.
 * 2. Each returned configuration increments `attempted_configuration_count`.
 *    @ref ModelConfigurationValidator checks policy, parameter layout, optimizer
 *    dimension, and method-specific constraints before training starts.
 * 3. `evaluate_configuration` trains and validates the configuration. The
 *    returned mean must be finite and variance finite and non-negative.
 * 4. @ref ConfigurationScoringCriterion combines natural-direction performance
 *    and enabled cost terms into a finite lower-is-better score.
 * 5. A success enters @ref ModelSelectionState and produces successful
 *    @ref ConfigurationFeedback. A caught @ref InvalidConfigurationError or
 *    @ref ConfigurationEvaluationError produces failed feedback and a
 *    @ref ModelSelectionFailureRecord.
 * 6. Stopping strategies inspect feedback until the first reason is found. The
 *    remaining issued configurations are still evaluated. The entire ordered
 *    feedback batch reaches `ConfigurationSelector::tell()` before selection stops.
 * 7. If no criterion fires, the loop continues while `hasNext()` is true.
 *    Exhaustion produces @ref OptimizationTerminationReason::ConfigurationSelectorExhausted.
 * 8. The lowest-score successful configuration is passed to final training,
 *    then final test evaluation. Selection, final-training, and test metrics are
 *    combined in @ref ModelSelectionResult.
 *
 * Target and no-improvement conditions can therefore overshoot by the unprocessed
 * portion of an already issued batch. A maximum-configuration budget limits
 * batch cardinality before `ask()` and therefore stops at its exact bound.
 *
 * @section selection_space Search-space representation
 *
 * @ref ConfigurationSearchSpace is the Cartesian product of its axes. Each
 * @ref ConfigurationAxis owns a domain and borrows one mutable field of a stable
 * @ref ModelConfiguration. Axis tuple order defines genome order and grid
 * nesting. Duplicate field addresses are rejected.
 *
 * - @ref DiscreteDomain stores a non-empty ordered value vector. Repeated values
 *   occupy repeated positions.
 * - @ref CategoricalDomain stores unique identifier/value pairs in order.
 * - @ref ContinuousDomain stores finite inclusive bounds.
 *
 * The configuration owning bound fields must outlive the search space and
 * selector and must remain at the same address. Every returned model
 * configuration is a value copy taken after the selector assigns axis fields.
 *
 * @section selection_selectors Selector contracts
 *
 * @image html model_selection_strategies.svg "Configuration-selector and model-selection-stopping families."
 *
 * @ref GridConfigurationSelector enumerates a finite mixed-radix grid with the
 * last axis changing fastest. Continuous cardinality is
 * `ceil((upper-lower)/continuous_step_size)+1`; clamping the final point includes
 * the upper bound even when the interval length is not an exact multiple.
 * Grid enumeration proceeds independently of feedback, and grid exhaustion
 * supplies its limit.
 *
 * @ref RandomConfigurationSelector independently resamples every axis for every
 * output. @ref RandomWalkConfigurationSelector uniformly selects one axis per
 * output and resamples only that field, so elements within one batch are
 * sequential walk states. Both streams are unbounded and require an explicit
 * model-selection budget.
 *
 * @ref GeneticConfigurationSelector emits one engine generation through one or
 * more batches and advances only after complete generation feedback. Its state
 * and operators are described in @ref genetic_search_chapter.
 *
 * @section selection_validation Holdout validation
 *
 * @ref ValidationProtocol owns temporary training problems and optimizers while
 * borrowing the configured environment. Training evaluates every candidate on
 * `training_scenarios` in stored order with `training_runs_per_scenario`
 * replicas. The trained incumbent is then evaluated on `validation_scenarios`
 * with `validation_runs_per_scenario` replicas and policy regularization
 * excluded.
 *
 * The resulting @ref ConfigurationEvaluation contains the natural-direction
 * mean, population variance, and the sum of training and validation metrics.
 * Validation requires at least one finite objective sample. Its selection score
 * remains empty until @ref ModelSelection applies scoring.
 *
 * @section selection_kfold K-fold validation
 *
 * @ref KFoldCrossValidationProtocol concatenates configured training scenarios
 * followed by validation scenarios. A local `std::mt19937_64` seeded from
 * `random_seed` reproducibly permutes their indices. With \f$q\f$ scenarios and
 * \f$K\f$ folds, base size is \f$\lfloor q/K\rfloor\f$ and the first
 * \f$q\bmod K\f$ folds receive one extra scenario.
 *
 * Every fold constructs a fresh training optimizer on the complement and uses
 * its held-out fold for validation. If fold \f$k\f$ contributes \f$n_k\f$
 * validation samples with mean \f$\widehat J_k(c)\f$ and population variance \f$v_k\f$,
 * aggregation uses weighted first and second moments:
 *
 * \f[
 * \overline J(c)=\frac{\sum_kn_k\widehat J_k(c)}{\sum_kn_k},\qquad
 * v=\frac{\sum_kn_k\left(v_k+\widehat J_k(c)^2\right)}{\sum_kn_k}-\overline J(c)^2.
 * \f]
 *
 * A computed negative variance is clamped to zero after finiteness checks.
 * Metrics include training and validation work from every fold.
 *
 * @section selection_stopping Stopping state
 *
 * @ref ModelSelectionStoppingCriterion owns at most one strategy of each type
 * and checks them in caller order. @ref ModelSelectionBudgetCriterion counts
 * all attempted configurations, including failures. @ref ModelSelectionNoImprovementCriterion
 * processes successful feedback only and resets its counter when
 * `best_score-current_score > threshold`. @ref ModelSelectionTargetScoreCriterion
 * stops on a successful `score <= target_score`.
 *
 * Unbounded selectors require a budget strategy at construction. Grid selection
 * may run with an empty stopping vector and terminate by exhaustion.
 *
 * @section selection_final Final training and test
 *
 * @ref makeModelSelectionFunctions captures validation settings and test
 * scenarios by value while retaining the borrowed environment reference. Its
 * final-training callback concatenates training scenarios followed by validation
 * scenarios and uses `training_runs_per_scenario`. Its final-test callback uses
 * `validation_runs_per_scenario`, excludes policy regularization through the
 * protocol's evaluation operation, and returns objective samples in their
 * natural direction. The helper configures that direction as maximization.
 *
 * Failed attempts populate failure records. Successful attempts populate
 * `evaluated_configurations` and `selection_execution_metrics`. A partial
 * evaluation is retained in a failure record only when the callback returned it
 * before statistics or scoring were rejected. Selection finishing with zero
 * successful records throws `std::runtime_error`; final callback exceptions propagate.
 *
 * @see @ref genetic_search_chapter "Genetic configuration search"
 * @see @ref cost_validation_chapter "Computational cost and configuration validation"
 * @see @ref technical_chapters "Technical Chapters"
 */
